Z||000000||Philphine||10-17-2001||11:36 AM||||ever thought about how much you have in you fiero?<P>i read the $2002 challenge thread and looked at the web site. the whole idea is really interesting. i couldn't do it my self and come up with anything close to competitive. i'd have to farm out too much and i don't have the experience to see something in a junkyard and know i can use it for cheap. <P>i just like the idea of having a neat looking, good performing little something that has as a main bragging point the fact that i only have a small amount of cash invested in. i think i'll make low cost more of a goal (like it isn't already. imma cheapskate anyway) on at least one car.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||10-17-2001||12:22 PM||||I try not to think how much I have in my car... especially since I drive it just for fun and don't use it to commute or do much shopping.  I don't mean in modifications either!  Just in repair bills!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>The exterior/interior isn't perfect, but its awfully good and with a good wax job I think its showable, although not necessarily a winner (a few scratches, especially the front fascia from stones.)<BR> <BR>I'd really like to get some endine modifications done to it.  My biggest problem is I am not the best mechanic in the world, and do not have the major tools or facility to do any major engine work.  So it would start to cost a lot of $$ quickly to get into conversions or rebuilds.  Ah, but maybe someday (hopefully soon!)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR><P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formulasig.JPG">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||10-17-2001||12:34 PM||||I'm with you- don't want to think of the total investment. <P>[pondering]<BR>hmmm let's see: bought the car with 64k miles & damage in '95 for $4600, at least $2500 in paint/body, about $2000 in the new motor & tranny, etc... that's about $9k not considering any regular repairs or miscellaneous- ouch! I'd guess I've got well over $12k in the car by now.  Now what can I sell to pay for an Archie V8...?<BR>[/pondering]<P>------------------<BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 10-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||10-17-2001||01:07 PM||||I have $23.52 +tax for mine with every mod.<P>That inclues:<P>monchrome viper red paint<BR>polished aluminum wheels<BR>new motor<BR>new cradle<BR>all new mounts<BR>sunroof<BR>window tint<BR>subwoofer<BR>cd player<BR>etc.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Formula_sigx21.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||mshill||10-17-2001||01:18 PM||||I am actually doing this with my sons 85SE that needs restoring.  He bought it for $250.  I paid him $100 and swapped my mint wheels with bad rubber for his ok wheels and new rubber.  I got a free V6 and auto tranny with harness and computer on a cradle from terryk.  Then I hit the junkyard and picked up a steering column ($20), mint dash ($19), mint GT instrument cluster ($11), good condition seat covers ($50 for the set), 87 coupe front a rear fascias ($75), complete set of round molding including markers ($20), and picked up front fenders and rear quarters ($50).<P>We will do all the prep and painting ourselves (won't be show quality), drop the engine and swap the interior. After that new brakes, bushings and tires and it should be ready to roll.  My son of course will be putting in a good stereo and alarm system, but besides that I think we can do the entire thing for less than $1000.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||10-17-2001||02:26 PM||||My 88 is the same way.<P>$4000 for the car in 96<BR>$1300 for repaint<BR>$500 new leather steering wheel<BR>$300 control arms/ball joints/e brake<BR>$300 steering rack + labor<BR>$300 transmission repairs/labor<BR>$300 GT Sail panels<BR>$2100 3.1 L engine<BR>$300 front exhaust manifold<BR>$800 labor for engine<BR>$600 shocks/struts<BR>$150 GM radio rebuild<BR>$400 a/c conversion/electrical repairs<BR>$700 Gold Lace wheels/ head liner<BR>$400 tires<BR>$4000+ 3.4 L engine/injectors/water pump/starter<BR>$2000 new transmission, new brakes, bushings<BR>$500 Borla exhaust<BR>$200 wood grain dash & console panels<BR>$150 new GP CD/AM/FM radio<BR>$200 another steering rack<BR>Probably lots of things not added in like power coated intake and valve covers, chrome throttle body, new trunk gasket, periodic 4 whhel alignments, battery, new front fascia, various trim pieces, distributor, oil sending units, fuel rails, fuel pumps<P>This is why I don't beat on the car.<BR>||||reg||1
