Z||000009||Little Duce Coupe||10-17-2001||07:54 PM||||$4500 Original Purchase<BR>$350 for a broken spring in the pressure plate.<BR>$250 for clutch pedal arm, master and slave cylender.<BR>$1250 estimate to fix AC.. Told dealer to stuff it.<BR>$150 for new alternator... and a day of my time.<P>This is sounding pretty bad, except.....<P>I bought it as the second owner in 1991 with 14k original miles (still had stock tires).<P>It now has 125k miles on it...<P>That works out to be:<P>$525.oo a year or equal to one regular car payment.<BR>or...<BR>$21.00 a mile, Hmmm....<P>Thus my name... every mile was a hoot though.<P>------------------<BR>Little Duce Coupe<BR>"You Don't Know What She Costs"||||reg||12
Z||000010||AusFiero||10-17-2001||08:12 PM||||I had a bit over $32,000 in mine before the fire. Now I have an expensive, driveable but horrible looking and smelling mess. But at least I managed to buy it back from the insurance company for $2000 si I suppose currently thats all I have in it after the insurance payout. Well plus the $7000 I lost when the payout came.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero2.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
